### Inheritance 

one class acquire properties from another 

Inheritance allows one class (child/derived class) to acquire the properties and behavior (data members + member functions) of another class (parent/base class).

### Basic Syntax

class Base {
    // parent class
};

class Derived : access_specifier Base {
    // child class
};


#### TYPES OF Inheritance
1. Single Inheritance -> Ek base class → ek derived class
2.  Multiple Inheritance -> Ek derived class → do ya zyada base classes se
3.  Multilevel Inheritance -> Chain jaisa — Base → Derived1 → Derived2
4. Hierarchical Inheritance -> Ek base class → multiple derived classes
5. Hybrid Inheritance -> Do ya zyada types ka combination (jaise Multiple + Multilevel mix)


++++++++++++++++++++ Access Specifiers +++++++++++++

class Base {
private:
    int a;       // never accessible in Derived directly
protected:
    int b;       // accessible in Derived
public:
    int c;       // accessible in Derived
};

class Derived : public Base {
    void show() {
        // cout << a;   ❌ ERROR
        cout << b;      // ✅ works
        cout << c;      // ✅ works
    }
};

INSHORT WE CANT USE private
